# Local development environment template.
#
# The server has no local datastore — it talks to a self-hosted Convex backend
# over HTTP. Copy this file to .env (or .env.local, which is gitignored) and set
# the Convex connection below before running `bun run dev`. Stand up or point at
# a Convex backend per docs/DEPLOY-CONVEX.md.

PORT=3001

# Comma-separated CIDRs for reverse proxies whose X-Forwarded-For header may
# be trusted. Leave empty for direct/local development.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=127.0.0.1/32,::1/128

# ─── Convex backend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED. The server reaches its data layer through these vars
# (server/convex/client.ts). CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_URL is the backend URL; CONVEX_URL
# is read as a fallback when it is unset. CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_ADMIN_KEY
# authenticates the trusted server→Convex channel (generate/rotate it with the
# self-hosted Convex tooling — see docs/DEPLOY-CONVEX.md).
CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_URL=
CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_ADMIN_KEY=
# CONVEX_URL=

# ─── Filesystem paths ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
UPLOADS_DIR=./uploads
STATIC_DIR=./dist

# ─── AI credential encryption ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev auto-creates .tmp/secret.key. Production deployments must set
# INSTATIC_SECRET_KEY to the output of:
#
#   bun run scripts/generate-secret-key.ts
#
# INSTATIC_SECRET_KEY=
